# Gate D digest safety.
#
# The Gate D acceptance marker binds a SHA-256 computed over the *bytes on disk* of the
# frozen generator files and of the frozen Gate C2 protocol document. Git's autocrlf/eol
# conversion can silently rewrite those bytes (LF <-> CRLF) without `git status` reporting
# anything, which changes the digest and closes the training lock. That happened twice
# during this round — to research/tree_qc/gate_d_sampler.py and to
# research/tree_qc/gate_d_fingerprint.py — and was recovered from the stored blobs.
#
# `-text` disables all end-of-line conversion for the frozen research core, so the files
# are stored and checked out exactly as committed and a clean checkout reproduces both
# accepted digests.
research/tree_qc/gate_d_provenance.py  -text
research/tree_qc/gate_d_scene.py       -text
research/tree_qc/gate_d_geometry.py    -text
research/tree_qc/gate_d_generator.py   -text
research/tree_qc/gate_d_sampler.py     -text
research/tree_qc/gate_d_dataset.py     -text
research/tree_qc/gate_d_metrics.py     -text
research/tree_qc/gate_d_train.py       -text
research/tree_qc/gate_d_fingerprint.py -text
research/tree_qc/gate_d_diagnostic.py  -text
research/tree_qc/gate_d_lock.py        -text
research/tree_qc/reports/GATE_D_ACCEPTANCE.json -text
research/tree_qc/reports/GATE_C_CANONICAL_IDENTITY_PROTOCOL_V2.md -text

# Tree QC V2 feasibility round.
#
# The ROI library index records the SHA-256 of every stored artefact, and the
# library index's own digest is quoted in the bakeoff report, so the report can be
# traced to the exact bytes it was computed from. Git's autocrlf conversion can
# rewrite LF <-> CRLF on checkout without `git status` reporting anything, which
# breaks that chain silently. `-text` stores and checks out these files exactly as
# committed, so a clean checkout reproduces the digest the run recorded.
research/tree_qc_v2/** -text
